|name2 = Zeta Skanda
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Zeta Skanda''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Zeta Skanda is a unique type of rusher that specializes in status effects over damage.

To start, the general use of Skanda comes mainly in abusing short-ranged melee rushers like [[Boraphim]], [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]], and [[Shy Boy]] to afflict enemies up to 533 range with [[Weaken]] through his [[Wave Attack]]s. This is a very versatile role and can alleviate the pressure off troublesome backline and midrange supports such as [[Cala Maria]] or [[Ursamajor]] by cutting their damage in half. Additionally, his [[Conjure]] is very powerful and can give you a moment to rally your units whenever you're in a bind. The Conjure can also be used to support units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N]] by freezing enemies in a similar manner to the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt Cannon]], allowing them an opportunity to land a hit. This aspect, alongside Skanda's Weaken, can keep your rushers alive for many more rebounds, giving them great synergy with him.

His effective HP against target traits is very high, but so is his recharge rate compared to other rushers. Using him to burst down powerful enemies is strongly discouraged as a result; you will obtain the highest value by keeping him alive for as long as possible. This means that he doesn't have many bad matchups so long as there's an enemy that you can use to continuously launch Wave Attacks from, regardless of what that enemy is. [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]], their [[Barrier]]s specifically, are highly susceptible to this, making [[UltraBaaBaa]] an incredibly powerful opportunity to use Skanda on.

Take note: Despite Skanda having Sage Slayer, it only applies to his Weaken, meaning his Conjure’s Freeze is still susceptible to Sages’ passive ability to reduce the duration of status effects by 70%.

Despite how situational he may be, under the right circumstances, Zeta Skanda's support can be the difference between winning and losing.

